  "label": "The emotional distress of students reacting to a history teacher discussing the Holocaust is mapped onto the visual of two people covering their mouths in discomfort.",
  "description": "The text 'when your history teacher starts talking about the holocaust' is mapped onto the visual of two people (a man and a woman) covering their mouths and showing expressions of distress. This mapping suggests that the visual representation of emotional discomfort (distress) is being used to symbolize the overwhelming emotional reaction one might have to learning about the Holocaust in class. The visual material (distressed_people) is being analogically mapped to the textual material (text_chunk) to convey the idea that the subject matter is so emotionally heavy that it causes physical reactions.",
